  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed roof lights by reason of their combined size, siting, design, quantum would appear visually intrusive and out of keeping with the historic roofscape harming the external appearance of the Grade II Parish Rooms listed building and it's setting and to the surrounding Mitcham Cricket green conservation area, contrary to Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990, Chapter 16 of the NPPF, HC1 of the London Plan and D12.3, D12.4, D12.5 Merton Local Plan 2025",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed removal of rear pitched roof to create flat roof extension would materially alter the original external roof of the building resulting in harm the architectural interest and external appearance of the Grade II Parish Rooms listed building and it's setting and to the surrounding Mitcham Cricket green conservation area, contrary to Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990, Chapter 16 of the NPPF, HC1 of the London Plan and D12.3, D12.4, D12.5 Merton Local Plan 2025",
    "Reason : 3 - By reason of absence of satisfactory and detailed a heritage statement and detailed schedule of works, the proposal fails to describe the significance of the heritage asset and assess the impact of proposed works to the detriment of Grade II Parish Rooms listed building and it's setting. The proposal is contrary to Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990, Chapter 16 of the NPPF, HC1 of the London Plan and D12.3, D12.4, D12.5 Merton Local Plan 2025",
    "Reason : 4 - INFORMATIVE\r\nNote to Applicant\r\nIn accordance with paragraph 38 of the NPPF, The London Borough of Merton  (LBM) takes a positive and proactive approach to development proposals focused on solutions. LBM works with applicants/agents in a positive and proactive manner by:\r\n\"\tOffering a pre-application advice and duty desk service. \r\n\"\tWhere possible, suggesting solutions to secure a successful outcome.\r\n\"\tAs appropriate, updating applicants/agents of any issues that may arise in the processing of their application.\r\nIn this instance:\r\n\"\tThe application was not considered to comply with the provisions of the Development Plan and NPPF as submitted, and would have required substantial changes such that a new application would be required. \r\n\r\n\"\tThe applicant is advised to seek pre-application advice on any resubmission.\r\n"
  ],
